To reproduce:
1.  Start a new project with web support
2.  Replace the script in index.html with this code

`    if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
      window.addEventListener('flutter-first-frame', function () {
        navigator.serviceWorker.register('flutter_service_worker.js')
        .then((reg) => {
             navigator.serviceWorker.controller.postMessage('downloadOffline');
        });
      });
    }`

3.  Build the web project
4. Access build/web/index.html through a web server, and refresh the page to get the service worker to run downloadOffline.
5. Look at the network log in the browser.  Instead of loading real resource files, the service worker attempts to download files named "0" through "14".

I have uploaded the result of steps 1-3 to my web site at https://www.bradchristie.com/sample_web_project/

The bug is one line in downloadOffline,

`  for (var resourceKey in Object.keys(RESOURCES)) {`

should be

`  for (var resourceKey of Object.keys(RESOURCES)) {`

